{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <limits>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long my_gcd(long long a, long long b) {\n    a = llabs(a);\n    b = llabs(b);\n    while (b) {\n        long long temp = b;\n        b = a % b;\n        a = temp;\n    }\n    return a ? a : 1;\n}\n\nlong long my_lcm(long long a, long long b) {\n    return a / my_gcd(a, b) * b;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    if (y <= n) {\n        long long g = my_gcd(x, y);\n        while (g != 1) {\n            x /= g;\n            y /= g;\n            g = my_gcd(x, y);\n        }\n        cout << x << \"/\" << y;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    long long best_numer = 1, best_denom = 1;\n    double min_err = numeric_limits<double>::max();\n    \n    for (long long i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        long long L = my_lcm(i, y);\n        long long target = x * (L / y);\n        long long unit = L / i;\n        \n        // Floor approximation\n        long long q_floor = target / unit;\n        long long approx_floor = q_floor * unit;\n        double err_floor = abs(target - approx_floor) / (double)L;\n        \n        if (err_floor < min_err) {\n            min_err = err_floor;\n            best_numer = q_floor;\n            best_denom = i;\n        }\n        \n        // Ceiling approximation\n        long long q_ceil = (target + unit - 1) / unit;\n        long long approx_ceil = q_ceil * unit;\n        double err_ceil = abs(target - approx_ceil) / (double)L;\n        \n        if (err_ceil < min_err) {\n            min_err = err_ceil;\n            best_numer = q_ceil;\n            best_denom = i;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    long long g = my_gcd(best_numer, best_denom);\n    best_numer /= g;\n    best_denom /= g;\n    \n    cout << best_numer << \"/\" << best_denom;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static long my_gcd(long a, long b) {\n        a = Math.abs(a);\n        b = Math.abs(b);\n        while (b != 0) {\n            long temp = b;\n            b = a % b;\n            a = temp;\n        }\n        return a != 0 ? a : 1;\n    }\n\n    public static long my_lcm(long a, long b) {\n        return a / my_gcd(a, b) * b;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long x = scanner.nextLong();\n        long y = scanner.nextLong();\n        long n = scanner.nextLong();\n        \n        if (y <= n) {\n            long g = my_gcd(x, y);\n            while (g != 1) {\n                x /= g;\n                y /= g;\n                g = my_gcd(x, y);\n            }\n            System.out.println(x + \"/\" + y);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        long best_numer = 1;\n        long best_denom = 1;\n        double min_err = Double.MAX_VALUE;\n        \n        for (long i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            long L = my_lcm(i, y);\n            long target = x * (L / y);\n            long unit = L / i;\n            \n            // Floor approximation\n            long q_floor = target / unit;\n            long approx_floor = q_floor * unit;\n            double err_floor = Math.abs(target - approx_floor) / (double)L;\n            \n            if (err_floor < min_err) {\n                min_err = err_floor;\n                best_numer = q_floor;\n                best_denom = i;\n            }\n            \n            // Ceiling approximation\n            long q_ceil = (target + unit - 1) / unit;\n            long approx_ceil = q_ceil * unit;\n            double err_ceil = Math.abs(target - approx_ceil) / (double)L;\n            \n            if (err_ceil < min_err) {\n                min_err = err_ceil;\n                best_numer = q_ceil;\n                best_denom = i;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        long g = my_gcd(best_numer, best_denom);\n        best_numer /= g;\n        best_denom /= g;\n        \n        System.out.println(best_numer + \"/\" + best_denom);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00020203932945150882, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00022837892174720764, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -0.022442644461989403, -0.6583601832389832, -3.075552376685664e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.3854863431770355e-05, -0.003600901225581765, -0.006717006675899029, -0.1282557249069214, -4.291525328881107e-06, -0.04302902892231941, -0.0022199528757482767, -0.0004189328756183386, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.5616295058862306e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.00018523407925385982, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -3.909988299710676e-05, -1.6093124941107817e-05, 0.0, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -